  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Friendly Kitchen",
    "overview": "Thinnava is a food diary kept among friends, and the system is built to feel like a warm, uncluttered kitchen table rather than a review site. Every surface is about a person and what they said; nothing is about stars, photos or aggregate scores. The chef-cat mascot (the owner's own art, `ui-references/7.png`, used as alpha-matted cutouts `design/assets/cat-sitting.png` and `cat-peek.png`) is the brand and appears on identity moments: splash, welcome, profile setup and empty states, where the peeking cat's paws rest on the top edge of a card.\n\nStructure is Android Material 3 (top app bar, navigation bar with pill indicator, chips, bottom sheets, segmented control), and the brand arrives through theming: a cobalt-blue role set, soft rounded white cards, Fredoka for the friendly display voice and Nunito for everything read. The page ground is flat. The owner rejected gradients as \"vibecoded\"; depth comes from white surfaces lifting off a pale sky ground with soft, diffuse shadows.\n\nDensity is relaxed and one-handed: 48px touch targets, 52px primary buttons, an 18px screen gutter, one obvious primary action per screen.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Flat sky ground, white rounded cards and list surfaces on top.",
      "Fredoka display (600) for wordmark, headings and place names; Nunito body with heavy weights (700/800) for names and labels.",
      "Material 3 skeleton, brand via colour roles; one role set shared by every palette.",
      "Good / Okayish / Bad review pills in fixed semantic green / amber / red.",
      "The chef cat on identity and empty moments only."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Fixed Verdict Rule",
        "body": "Good is always green, Okayish always amber, Bad always red, in every palette and every screen. Brand colour never stands in for a verdict, and verdict colours never decorate.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Role Set Rule",
        "body": "Every colour on a screen comes from a role (`p`, `p-strong`, `pc`, `bg`, `surface`, `ink`...). New screens use roles, not hex values, so palettes stay swappable.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Fredoka speaks for the brand and for places (wordmark, headings, place names, big numerals); Nunito carries everything else. Never set body copy or buttons in Fredoka.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Soft Lift Rule",
        "body": "Depth is white on sky plus a diffuse navy-tinted shadow. Strokes are inset hairlines (1-1.5px `hairline`), never heavy borders.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** keep the ground flat: Mist by default; Art or Solid treatment pending the owner's decision.",
      "**Do** lead every entry with who and where, then loved / didn't like / price, with the review pill in the footer.",
      "**Do** use the fixed Good / Okayish / Bad pills for every verdict, in every palette.",
      "**Do** set place names, headings and the wordmark in Fredoka 600; everything else in Nunito.",
      "**Do** use roles (`p`, `pc`, `surface`, `ink`) rather than raw hex so palettes remain swappable.",
      "**Do** show the chef cat on identity and empty moments, peeking over a card's top edge.",
      "**Do** mark private entries with the lock \"Only you\"."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use gradients on grounds or surfaces; the owner rejected them.",
      "**Don't** use hard offset shadows or heavy borders; lift is a soft blurred shadow, strokes are inset hairlines.",
      "**Don't** show stars or numeric scores as the app's own rating, and no rating summaries; stars appear only beside Google's figure.",
      "**Don't** add photos to entries or cards.",
      "**Don't** recolour verdict pills with brand colours, or use verdict colours as decoration (the mockup's red \"loved\" heart is a known conflict with this rule, not a pattern to copy).",
      "**Don't** set body copy or buttons in Fredoka."
    ]
  }
